_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 25
---
order: 25
---
short_label: V.25
---
statement: If four magnitudes are proportional, then the sum of the greatest and the least is greater than the sum of the remaining two.
---
proof:

Let the four magnitudes *AB, CD, E,* and *F* be proportional so that *AB* is to *CD* as *E* is to *F,* and let *AB* be the greatest of them and *F* the least.

I say that the sum of *AB* and *F* is greater than the sum of *CD* and *E.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="300" height="150" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="V.25 diagram" src="propV25.gif"/></noscript>
